name: unreachable-after-exit
prereqs: [none — a self-contained block scan]
invariant: only the straight-line tail after a DIRECT unconditional
  `Exit` (or a function-body `Return`) is dropped; conditional exits
  and every non-exit statement are untouched.
scope: offered to all (estree owner, c, go, perl, python, rust, sh,
  zig, glsl)
updates: none (first offer)
